<article class="env-lemma" id="0B7H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B7H">Lemma <span data-tag="0B7H">42.38.7</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $\mathcal{E}$ be a locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of rank $r$. Let $0 \leq p \leq r$. Then the rule that to $f : X' \to X$ assigns $c_ p(f^*\mathcal{E}) \cap - : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X') \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - p}(X')$ is a bivariant class of degree $p$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Lemmas <a href="/tag/02U7" data-tag="02U7">42.38.3</a>, <a href="/tag/02U9" data-tag="02U9">42.38.4</a>, <a href="/tag/02U8" data-tag="02U8">42.38.5</a>, and <a href="/tag/0B7G" data-tag="0B7G">42.38.6</a> and Definition <a href="/tag/0B76" data-tag="0B76">42.33.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>